{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"SegmentSpecEncoding","title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Segment","title":"Sending to Segment"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-RudderStack","title":"Sending to RudderStack"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Customerio-Data-Pipelines","title":"Sending to Customer.io Data Pipelines"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", writes it, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" of the workspace’s region ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Pipelines API’s "},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the workspace’s region ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the key as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bearer token and "},{"code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 2,500 calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_…"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_…"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"text":" call or traits are sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes in the spec’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"text":" fields (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os"},{"text":"), with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device.id"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"advertisingId"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"},{"text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":" from the request unless the call has one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even beside ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"},{"text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" takes the place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each endpoint counts a user per "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch has no session, so it goes out under its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which the record keeps, and drops most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is most likely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User Deleted"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User Suppressed"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Device Deleted"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan when the destination is made."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"title":"batchLimit","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder\/batchlimit","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The Segment spec’s limits on one request, which Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accept: 2,500 calls, 500,000 bytes of body, and 31,999 bytes of one call.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Customer.io Data Pipelines source of ","type":"text"},{"code":"apiKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"workspace in ","type":"text"},{"code":"region","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"code":"transport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"waits of ","type":"text"},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"customerIO"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"apiKey"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding16CustomerIORegionO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CustomerIORegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding20CustomerIOSetupErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CustomerIOSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/customerio(apikey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","title":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecEncodingError":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecencodingerror","title":"SegmentSpecEncodingError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecEncodingError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecEncodingError"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder":{"title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of the Segment spec’s batch call, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to Segment, RudderStack, Customer.io Data Pipelines, or another endpoint that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes Segment’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v1\/batch"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}],"url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}]},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"title":"segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/segment(writekey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Segment source of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"writeKey"},{"type":"text","text":", in a workspace in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"type":"text","text":", through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"segment"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writeKey"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text"